-- e3d-io group gate: read back a GPWL / GPSET / GPITEM chain that e3d-io wrote, in a
-- real E3D 3.1 Design TTY session. Read-only: no SAVEWORK, no QUIT -- the l3_suite
-- driver's wrapper owns the session.
--
-- Rendered by tools/e3d/group_gate.ps1 from this template; the refnos come from
-- `e3d-group-gate`'s JSON on the project copy.
--
-- The question this gate exists for is Q3: a GPSET whose members are GPITEMs carrying a
-- GPREF must expand to the real elements. Measured on APS 250204 (2026-11-08): `Q MEM` on
-- the GPSET prints the GPITEM itself (`1 GPITEM 1 =<ref>`), not the element its GPREF
-- names. Q2 therefore asserts the GPITEM member line, and Q4 separately proves the GPREF
-- target is a real design element E3D accepts.
--
-- One ALPHA LOG block per question: a block's log is written only at ALPHA LOG END, so an
-- unhandled error loses that block's log and no other. Every navigation and every risky Q
-- is followed by handle any.
--
-- The last block is the driver's own query log: `l3_suite --check-driver` reads
-- `<macro name>.log` next to the macro, and reports the whole run as failed when that file
-- is missing. It carries one line of summary, and it is written last so its presence also
-- means every block above reached ALPHA LOG END.

ALPHA LOG "{{LOGDIR}}/00_project.log" OVER
$P GATE-00-BEGIN
Q PROJ
Q MDB
$P GATE-00-END
ALPHA LOG END

ALPHA LOG "{{LOGDIR}}/10_gpwl.log" OVER
$P GATE-10-BEGIN
={{GPWL}}
handle any
  $P GATE-10-NAV-ERROR $!!error.text
elsehandle none
  Q REF
  Q TYPE
  Q OWNER
  Q NAME
  Q MEM
endhandle
$P GATE-10-END
ALPHA LOG END

ALPHA LOG "{{LOGDIR}}/20_gpset_items.log" OVER
$P GATE-20-BEGIN
={{GPSET_ITEMS}}
handle any
  $P GATE-20-NAV-ERROR $!!error.text
elsehandle none
  Q REF
  Q TYPE
  Q OWNER
  Q NAME
  Q MEM
endhandle
$P GATE-20-END
ALPHA LOG END

-- The GPITEM itself: what E3D thinks it is, and who owns it.
--
-- `Q GPREF` is NOT asked: measured on APS 250204, that question takes the whole session
-- down (exit 0xC0000005) because GPREF is not in E3D's dictionary. `Q ATT` is the legal
-- substitute; it prints Name/Type/Lock/Owner/Description/SItem and no GPREF, so the
-- GPREF value is verified on the write side (e3d-io reads it back) and by Q4 below.
ALPHA LOG "{{LOGDIR}}/30_gpitem.log" OVER
$P GATE-30-BEGIN
={{GPITEM_HERE}}
handle any
  $P GATE-30-NAV-ERROR $!!error.text
elsehandle none
  Q REF
  Q TYPE
  Q OWNER
  Q ATT
endhandle
$P GATE-30-END
ALPHA LOG END

-- The real element the same-db GPITEM points at, so the gate can compare: this is what the
-- GPSET's expansion should have printed.
ALPHA LOG "{{LOGDIR}}/40_target.log" OVER
$P GATE-40-BEGIN
={{TARGET_HERE}}
handle any
  $P GATE-40-NAV-ERROR $!!error.text
elsehandle none
  Q REF
  Q TYPE
  Q NAME
  Q OWNER
endhandle
$P GATE-40-END
ALPHA LOG END

-- The rules set: its member list is the GPITEM written explicitly; the SCOSEL is what
-- E3D would evaluate. `Q MEM` here is the explicit half only.
ALPHA LOG "{{LOGDIR}}/50_gpset_rules.log" OVER
$P GATE-50-BEGIN
={{GPSET_RULES}}
handle any
  $P GATE-50-NAV-ERROR $!!error.text
elsehandle none
  Q REF
  Q TYPE
  Q OWNER
  Q MEM
endhandle
$P GATE-50-END
ALPHA LOG END

-- The driver's query log (see the note at the top): `<macro name>.log`, written last.
ALPHA LOG "{{QUERYLOG}}" OVER
$P GATE-SUMMARY-BEGIN
$P GATE-SUMMARY all six blocks reached ALPHA LOG END
$P GATE-SUMMARY-END
ALPHA LOG END

$P GATE-DONE
